      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, this function is to generate unique ID. \n\nIt is worth discussing whether there is a possibility that a Socket ID generated from a 64-bit random number can be duplicated among connected sockets, but considering the number of connected sockets that a device can have, the possibility is very low. Therefore, we did not perform a separate duplication check. We are also considering generating a 64-bit random number and assigning it without a duplication check when adding an RFCOMM offload socket. If duplicated socket ID is tried to open, offload stack or HAL will return error anyway.",
